But there is special imp twist int this story

If in any expression we have BYTE, SHORT or CHAR 
type of operands the they will be automatically upgarded 
to INT before solving the expression.

This is because the compiler of java has been designed
in such a way that it operates in much faster way on INTEGERS.


EXAMPLE:
byte a=10;
byte b=20;
byte c;
c=a+b; //Error :lossy conv from int to byte

there are 2 solutions :

1.
c=(byte)(a+b);

2.int c= a+b;

Which of the solution is more reliable:

Answer : second solution is reliable ,

